concept or treat it as revocable. **CC0** is engineered around this: waiver, then a fallback permissive license if the waiver fails, then a covenant not to assert. Caveats to carry honestly: CC0 expressly does *not* license patent/trademark rights (why Fedora reclassified CC0 as not-allowed for *code* in 2022; data/content still fine), and FSF does not recommend CC0 for software. Sources: https://Wiki.CreativeCommons.org/images/6/69/CC0_Jurisdiction_Survey.pdf ; https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=30556049\n\n## Scope\n\n#5977 keeps public domain and CC0 as separate taxonomy entries; this follow-up decides the **storage normalization**:\n\n- A user selecting \"public domain\" is stored as `CC0-1.0` for content and `0BSD` (or Unlicense) for code — never as a bare \"public domain\" string.\n- One sentence of UI copy explaining why, in plain language.\n- What the registry and the combination checker see (the normalized SPDX identifier only).\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA normalization rule + UI copy, adopted by the taxonomy spec.\n","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5